mode: "100644"
text: "# Content audit 2026 — verified\n\n*Method is stable; re-verify platform/format specifics quarterly.*\n\n## What it is (and isn't)\nA content audit is a **retrospective reality-check.** Where **strategy is forward-looking** (goals,\npillars, schedule), the audit is **retrospective** — it checks how effectively you're *executing* that\nplan, then **informs a smarter one.** The trap it breaks: **activity isn't progress.** Plenty of accounts\nlook busy — daily reels, carousels, likes trickling in, followers inching up — while **nothing actually\nmoves.** The audit shows what's happening **beneath the surface** (what gets *saved* vs skipped, when the\naudience shows up) so you adjust *what* and *when*.\n\n## Scope of THIS skill\nThe **content + pillars + voice + profile** slice. It **routes out**: rivals → `competitor-analysis`;\nthe metric definitions/measurement → `analytics-and-reporting`; profile execution → `profile-optimization`.\nThe audit *reads* native analytics; it doesn't re-derive them.\n\n## Score on signal, not vanity\nJudge content on **saves, shares, replies** + the **goal-mapped KPI** — these \"signal algorithm-worthy\ncontent far more reliably than impressions or follower counts.\" A high-*like* post can be low-value, and\na modest-like post can be a quiet winner. Surface **top + bottom performers AND the patterns** (by\nformat, posting time, pillar).\n\n## The core decision: keep / kill / refresh\n- **KEEP / scale** — proven winners and high-leverage formats → double down (→ `content-recycling`).\n- **KILL / cut** — chronic underperformers, off-brand posts, dead or cross-posted non-native formats.\n- **REFRESH / revive** — good-but-dated or underseen content → update and re-publish.\nPlatform-native formats (vertical video, carousels) beat cross-posted static — flag cross-posts to\nrefresh or kill.\n\n## Diagnose pillars, voice & profile\n- **Pillar coverage:** map ~90 days of output to your **content pillars**; find **over/under-served**\n  pillars and **whitespace** (→ `content-pillars`).\n- **Voice drift — both ways:** are posts drifting **off-brand**? Or are well-performing posts a signal the\n  **brand voice should evolve** toward what's working? (→ `voice-builder`.)\n- **Profile fundamentals (compound, zero spend):** clear bio with keywords, working/strategic links,\n  pinned/featured posts showcasing winners, consistent handle/visuals (→ `profile-optimization`).\n- **Cadence:** posting frequency by platform — consistent without ghosting or overwhelming.\n\n## Window, frequency, output\nPull **~90 days** (3–6 months) of data. **Deep audit quarterly** (catches drift) + **light monthly**\nbenchmarks; small brands ~6-monthly; run one after any **major change** (rebrand, platform launch,\ncampaign, algorithm shift). Output = **strengths / weaknesses / opportunities** + **quick wins vs\nlong-term**, with **owners + timelines.** Don't let it become a **spreadsheet graveyard** — it must\nbecome an action plan that feeds the strategy, recycling queue, and profile.\n"
